<section class="home-sections Visibility enhances">
	<div class="container ">
		<div class="row">
			<div class="col-md-12 heighlighted-words text-white">
				<p>Processes generates data but unfortunately it is not visible, and therefore we don’t use it. The fact is that they can add huge amount of value to our business. They enable us to understand where, what, and why of our operations. Actions taken based on these understanding could drive our productivity, profitability and delivery resulting in improved value propositions. When you convert your business processes into a value creating process then there is nothing called an overhead.</p>
				
				<div class="text-center">
				<a href="#" class="btn btn-light btn-opiam btn-learnmore">Learn More <span class="icon-keyboard_arrow_right"></span></a>
				</div>
				
			</div>
		</div>
	</div>
</section>






<section class="home-sections brings-out-that-visibility-pic-bg">
<div class="container-fluid ">
	<div class="row">
		<div class="col-md-12 heighlighted-words" style="padding-top:0px;">
				<h2 class="text-upppercase text-center">Visibility should enhance perception <br/>deepen our
understanding, <br/>and give us Insights</h2>
			</div>
	</div>
	</div>
	
	
	
	<div class="container ">
	<div class="row">
		
		<div class="col-md-6 text-center" data-aos-easing="ease" data-aos-delay="300" data-aos="fade-up">
			<img src="images/d-rendering-robot-working-notebook-factory-robot-factory-108809488.jpg" width="" height="" alt="" />
		</div>
		<div class="col-md-6  " data-aos-easing="ease" data-aos-delay="600" data-aos="fade-up">
			<div class="brings-out-content">
				<h3 class="text-upppercase heading-decor">Opiam brings out that visibility</h3>
				<p>Imagine a cockpit in an aircraft without any instruments, how do you expect the pilot to navigate the flight. It could be the same for the CEO’s who are running an organisation  without the visibility of their operations. Huge amount of information missed our eyes because there was no visibility. Representing data in a few charts and graphs on a dashboard does not add any value, visibility means the ability to see the underlying causes and effects of our performance, which enhances our perception, deepen our understanding and give us new insights</p>
				<p>Opiam can dive into the data and bring out that critical visibility. Without data in its meaningful form we work on intuitions. Intuitions are derived from  past experience  while today organisations derive knowledge from realtime data.</p>
				<a href="#" class="btn btn-light btn-opiam btn-learnmore">Learn More <span class="icon-keyboard_arrow_right"></span></a>
			</div>
		</div>
		
	</div>
</div>
</section>


<section class="home-sections anything-connot-bed text-white">
	<div class="container-fluid ">

		<div class="row">
			
			<div class="col-md-12  anything-bga" data-aos-easing="ease" data-aos-delay="300" data-aos="fade-up" >
				<h2 class="text-upppercase heading-decor text-center">Anything that cannot be Measured<br/> cannot be managed</h2>
			</div>
			
		</div>
	</div>
	<div class="container ">

	<div class="row">
		<div class="col-md-12" style="height:100px;">
			&nbsp;
		</div>
		<div class="col-md-6 anything-bgs2" data-aos-easing="ease" data-aos-delay="900" data-aos="fade-up">
			<div class="anything-bg2-wrpr3">
			<h3 class="text-upppercase heading-decor small-line">Opiam improves performance</h3>
				<div class="content" data-aos-easing="ease" data-aos-delay="900" data-aos="fade-up">
				<p>Like a pilot who monitors the instruments in his cockpit to navigate the flight, the CEO’s should have a dashboard of measurements that enable him to navigate to the targeted outcomes of profitability, return on investment etc.. The instruments in the cockpit tells the pilot what lever needs to move and how much to move to control the air speed, the altitude, landing and various other parameters while flying.</p>
				<p>Similarly the measures in the CEO’s dashboard should tell the story of performance of his operations, the actions that he needs to take to achieve the desired outcome.</p>
				<p >A bunch of stand alone measures in the dashboard by itself does not tell you the story unless it is linked through a series of lead and lag measures.</p>
				
				<p>The lag measures tell us the results of the actions while the lead measure tell us what caused the result.</p>
				
				<p>The lag measure tell us the variation from the target or baseline while the lead measure tell us what caused the variation.</p><p> Measures give us control.</p>
				
				<p>Opiam gives you control by telling the story of performance through a series of lead and lag measures on your dashboard. It is by knowing where action is required (lead measure) and by seeing the result of that action (lag measure)  we  improve performance</p>
				
				<a href="#" class="btn btn-light btn-opiam btn-learnmore">Learn More <span class="icon-keyboard_arrow_right"></span></a>
				</div>
			</div>
		</div>
		<div class="col-md-6  anything-bgs" data-aos-easing="ease" data-aos-delay="600" data-aos="fade-up">
			<div class="anything-bg2-wrpr3" style="padding-top:50px;">
				<img class="" src="images/Opiam-improves-performance.jpg?v1" width="" height="" alt="" />
			</div>
			
			
		</div>
		
		
		
	</div>
</div>

</section>






